text:
Wait, I changed the include comment alignment by adding a space. Originally:
```
#include <fstream> // std::ofstream
#include <ostream> // std::ostream
```
Now:
```
#include <fstream>  // std::ofstream
#include <iostream> // std::cerr
#include <ostream>  // std::ostream
```
clang-format with AlignTrailingComments would align them. Let me check the style json. Actually clang-format usually aligns trailing comments to the same column. The original had single space for both because they were the same length (fstream/ostream both 9 chars? `<fstream>` 9, `<ostream>` 9). Adding `<iostream>` (10) means alignment changes. clang-format will align. I manually aligned to the longest (`<iostream>`). Good, but let me verify with clang-format after.

Now command_lint.cc.

